and its reserved\n  resources, and the last-activity values match the notebook controller's\n  activity tracking.\n- Given a project with completed pipeline runs, when an administrator opens\n  the stale pipeline-run report, then the report lists completed runs older\n  than the configured age threshold together with their retained artifacts,\n  and the entries match Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Given the stale-run age threshold is configurable, when an administrator\n  changes the threshold, then the stale pipeline-run report reflects the new\n  threshold without requiring code changes.\n- Given either report is displayed, when an administrator exports it, then a\n  CSV file is produced whose rows match the on-screen report contents.\n- Given the reports are used, when an administrator reviews cluster state,\n  then no resources have been modified or deleted by the reporting feature\n  (read-only reporting).\n- Given a project with no idle workbenches or stale runs, when the reports\n  are opened, then they render empty states without errors.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n  reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n  tracking — covered by this epic.\n- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n  run metadata — covered by this epic.\n- HLR-3 (P2): CSV export of either report — covered by this epic; bundled\n  because it is a thin increment on the same report surface the P1 work\n  builds, not an independently deferrable feature.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32170,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83f4eec66f291850","agent_id":"a2b5ca635b570b06f","session_id":"2f248c86-604e-49da-86f8-c3023caf7896","uuid":"e1455a49-9fec-4705-8b3e-5c3fd3850a8a","times