{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92da5bcac726cbf6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n3\tepic_count: 2\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition: RHAISTRAT-9016 — Idle resource reporting in the web console\n11\t\n12\tThe strategy asks for two read-only administrator reports in the RHOAI web\n13\tconsole — idle workbenches per project and stale pipeline runs — plus CSV\n14\texport and documentation. The strategy explicitly states the underlying data\n15\talready exists (notebook controller activity tracking, Kubeflow Pipelines run\n16\tmetadata) and lists no open questions, so the only active component is the web\n17\tconsole; the two data-source components are passive.\n18\t\n19\t**Triage outcome:** not below-threshold. Although the code work is a single\n20\tcomponent and team, the scope spans two architecturally distinct work streams\n21\t— console code implementation (HLR-1/2/3) and substantive documentation\n22\tauthoring with new doc topics (HLR-4, including safe-reclamation guidance) —\n23\twhich warrant separate PR review cycles. Full decomposition follows.\n24\t\n25\t## Epic List\n26\t\n27\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n28\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E002 | Document the idle and stale resource reports and safe reclamation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Docs | P2 |\n31\t\n32\t## Dependency DAG\n33\t\n34\t```mermaid\n35\tgraph TD\n36\t    E001[\"E001 — Idle and stale resource reports (Implementation, P1)\"] --> E002[\"E002 — Documentation (docs-authoring, P2)\"]\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t## DAG Justification\n40\t\n41\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n42\t|------|------|-----------|\n43\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics) | The documentation describes the reports as built (columns, thresholds, export behavior, reclamation steps); it cannot be authored or technically reviewed accurately before the console reporting implementation is complete. |\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n46\t\n47\t| HLR | Priority | Epic | Notes |\n48\t|-----|----------|------|-------|\n49\t| HLR-1 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Per-project idle-workbench report sourced from notebook controller activity tracking |\n50\t| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Stale pipeline-run report sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata |\n51\t| HLR-3 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | CSV export bundled with the reports: it is a thin increment on the same report UI surface and shares the reports' data, so it is not independently deferrable (Step 4 priority-split rule does not apply) |\n52\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E002 | Substantive new doc topics — separate work-product stream (docs-authoring) |\n53\t\n54\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n55\t\n56\t## Boundary Decisions\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-1 + HLR-2 in one epic:** both reports are the same logical change —\n59\t  per-project idle/stale resource reporting — on the same component (web\n60\t  console), same team (RHOAI Dashboard), same work-product type (code), and\n61\t  the same console reporting surface. HLR-3 applies to \"either report\",\n62\t  further coupling the surface. Splitting would make two epics build the same\n63\t  reporting surface with an artificial serialization edge.\n64\t- **No Investigation epics:** the strategy lists \"Open Questions: None\", has\n65\t  no risks/assumptions tables, no pending reviews, no conditional ADRs. How\n66\t  the console reads last-activity timestamps and run metadata (exact API/CR\n67\t  surface) is an implementation detail the Dashboard team resolves when\n68\t  starting work — captured as acceptance criteria on E001, not a genuine\n69\t  unknown.\n70\t- **Passive components:** Notebook controller (canonical component\n71\t  `Notebooks`, owning team Workbenches) and Kubeflow Pipelines (canonical\n72\t  component `Data Science Pipelines`, owning team RHOAI Pipelines) need no\n73\t  code changes — the strategy states the data exists. Validation that the\n74\t  reports match those data sources is an acceptance criterion on E001; no\n75\t  separate validation epics since the consuming (Dashboard) team performs the\n76\t  validation.\n77\t\n78\t## Component Mapping\n79\t\n80\t| Strategy term | Canonical component | Status |\n81\t|---------------|---------------------|--------|\n82\t| RHOAI web console | Dashboard | Active — all code changes |\n83\t| Notebook controller | Notebooks | Passive — data source, no code changes |\n84\t| Kubeflow Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | Passive — data source, no code changes |\n85\t\n86\tAll components exist in `.context/architecture-context/` (dashboard.md,\n87\tnotebooks.md, data-science-pipelines.md); no new-component onboarding chain\n88\tis needed, and the Dashboard repo is already Konflux-onboarded.\n89\t\n90\t## Health Warnings\n91\t\n92\t- **Missing strategy sections:** the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n93\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n94\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the\n95\t  HLRs; team assignments were taken from architecture context owning-team\n96\t  fields. Human verification of these inferred values is recommended.\n97\t- **Affected Components is a bare list** without owner/change columns; the\n98\t  active/passive classification above is inferred from the problem statement\n99\t  (\"the data exists; it is just not surfaced anywhere\").\n100\t- **Docs team assumption:** the strategy names no documentation owner; the\n101\t  `RHOAI Docs` team for the `Documentation` component is inferred from\n102\t  platform naming conventions.\n103\t- No priority inversions detected; no scope traps (out-of-scope items —\n104\t  automated reclamation and cost/chargeback — are respected in epic scope and\n105\t  docs acceptance criteria).\n106\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7da6eb140ceffd1","agent_id":"a5d1499eac38fe625","session_id":"2f248c86-604e-49da-86f8-c3023caf7896","uuid":"ca394b6f-a94a-4c99-b7a3-8fae37eb0da3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:48:49.570Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92da5bcac726cbf6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
