{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3d8a2d3304186f7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers read-only administrator reports in the RHOAI web console\n34\tthat surface idle and stale resources per project, so administrators can see\n35\twhere capacity is being held unused and reclaim it with confidence. Two\n36\treports are built on one console reporting surface: an idle-workbench report\n37\tsourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking, and a stale\n38\tpipeline-run report sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata. Either\n39\treport can be exported as CSV.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Per-project idle-workbench report in the console listing, for each\n44\t  workbench: last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n45\t  tracking), owner, and reserved resources.\n46\t- Per-project stale pipeline-run report in the console listing completed\n47\t  pipeline runs older than a configurable age threshold, together with their\n48\t  retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n49\t- Administrator-configurable stale-run age threshold for the pipeline-run\n50\t  report.\n51\t- CSV export of either report, matching the on-screen data.\n52\t- Console presentation is project-scoped (reports are viewed per data science\n53\t  project).\n54\t- Reporting is strictly read-only: no automated reclamation or deletion of\n55\t  resources, and no cost/chargeback calculations (both out of scope for the\n56\t  strategy).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given a project containing workbenches with differing activity, when an\n61\t  administrator opens the idle-workbench report, then the report lists each\n62\t  workbench with its last activity timestamp, its owner, and its reserved\n63\t  resources, and the last-activity values match the notebook controller's\n64\t  activity tracking.\n65\t- Given a project with completed pipeline runs, when an administrator opens\n66\t  the stale pipeline-run report, then the report lists completed runs older\n67\t  than the configured age threshold together with their retained artifacts,\n68\t  and the entries match Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n69\t- Given the stale-run age threshold is configurable, when an administrator\n70\t  changes the threshold, then the stale pipeline-run report reflects the new\n71\t  threshold without requiring code changes.\n72\t- Given either report is displayed, when an administrator exports it, then a\n73\t  CSV file is produced whose rows match the on-screen report contents.\n74\t- Given the reports are used, when an administrator reviews cluster state,\n75\t  then no resources have been modified or deleted by the reporting feature\n76\t  (read-only reporting).\n77\t- Given a project with no idle workbenches or stale runs, when the reports\n78\t  are opened, then they render empty states without errors.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n83\t  reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n84\t  tracking — covered by this epic.\n85\t- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n86\t  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n87\t  run metadata — covered by this epic.\n88\t- HLR-3 (P2): CSV export of either report — covered by this epic; bundled\n89\t  because it is a thin increment on the same report surface the P1 work\n90\t  builds, not an independently deferrable feature.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7da6eb140ceffd1","agent_id":"a5d1499eac38fe625","session_id":"2f248c86-604e-49da-86f8-c3023caf7896","uuid":"da168efe-033f-4ccd-9934-0986d046fd0c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:48:52.938Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3d8a2d3304186f7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
