umentation must not\n50\t  imply automated reclamation (out of scope for this strategy).\n51\t- Screenshots and captions reflecting the reports as built.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given the reporting capability is implemented, when the documentation is\n56\t  published, then topics exist that explain both reports, their per-project\n57\t  presentation, the configurable stale-run age threshold, and CSV export.\n58\t- Given an administrator wants to reclaim capacity, when they follow the\n59\t  documentation, then safe manual reclamation steps for idle workbenches and\n60\t  stale pipeline runs are described accurately.\n61\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented console\n62\t  reports, and any discrepancies found in review are corrected before\n63\t  publication.\n64\t- The documentation does not describe automated reclamation/deletion or\n65\t  cost/chargeback functionality (both out of scope).\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps —\n70\t  covered by this epic.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7da6eb140ceffd1","agent_id":"a5d1499eac38fe625","session_id":"2f248c86-604e-49da-86f8-c3023caf7896","uuid":"cf85fec6-d324-427f-b28b-55efa2c39704","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:48:53.647Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-910bb7217d75bdeb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
