encies. No circular or invalid edges, no konflux-onboarding or license-validation epics (so rules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints don't apply), no conditional branch files. No data/artifact dependency is missing from the DAG: E002's only input is the implemented feature, captured by the E001 edge. Critical path length 2 matches the S-strategy heuristic (1-2).\n25\t\n26\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n27\tE001: component Dashboard, team RHOAI Dashboard — matches the architecture context owning team. E002: component Documentation, team RHOAI Docs. Each epic is a single component/team tuple. HLR-1 + HLR-2 are correctly bundled as one logical change (same console reporting surface, same team, HLR-3 couples them further); splitting would duplicate the surface. No scope duplication between E001 and E002 — E001 is code, E002 is content authoring, so there is no work-product type mixing (the docs work is properly separated into its own epic). E001's scope (two list views on one reporting surface, a config threshold, CSV export) fits within a single sprint; no oversized epic.\n28\t\n29\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n30\tBoth epics are typed Implementation and both produce concrete artifacts (console feature; published doc topics). No Investigation epics — justified: the strategy lists \"Open Questions: None\", and the strategy's data-availability claims (notebook controller activity tracking, KFP run metadata retention) are corroborated by the architecture context files, so the remaining API-surface detail is an implementation concern correctly captured as acceptance criteria rather than a gating unknown. No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set, and no epic lists an Investigation dependency, so no gating metadata issues.\n31\t\n32\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n33\tBoth epics are Implementation type and both carry `ai_signals` (the 9-signal rubric) with `investigation_signals: null` — type-appropriate. E001: `open_questions: 1` is consistent with the strategy's empty open-questions list; `architecture_claims: 1` is corroborated — notebooks.md documents activity tracked per kernel and data-science-pipelines.md documents the KFP v2 REST API with runs surfaced in the Dashboard and artifacts in object storage; `existing_foundation: 1` matches extension of the existing console; `change_specificity: 0` is defensible given the strategy lacks Given/When/Then ACs and NFRs (noted in Health Warnings). E002: `human_process_gates: -1` is consistent with the mandatory technical-review AC; `change_specificity: 1` fits a docs epic whose subject is the completed implementation. Signal rationales in both ai-signals files match the frontmatter values. Score arithmetic not checked (computed by the pipeline).\n34\t\n35\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n36\tE001 has six testable Given/When/Then ACs covering both reports, data-source fidelity, the configurable threshold, CSV export matching on-screen data, read-only behavior, and empty states. E002 has four ACs including the Rule-mandated technical-review-against-implementation AC for docs-authoring, plus an explicit out-of-scope guard. No replacement epic exists (new feature), so no rollback/feature-flag AC is required; no konflux chain exists, so no build-pipeline AC is required. No AC is a misfiled schedule constraint or external timing risk. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID (E002 refers to \"the console reporting implementation\" generically).\n37\t\n38\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n39\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: both reports, per-project presentation, configurable age threshold, CSV export, documentation with safe reclamation steps, and the out-of-scope boundaries (no automated reclamation, no cost/chargeback) are respected in both epic scopes and E002's ACs. The problem statement's \"reclaim capacity with confidence\" intent is carried into E002's safe-reclamation guidance. The strategy has no risks, assumptions, or open questions to drop (it declares none), and the decomposition's Health Warnings correctly surface the strategy's missing sections (no Impacted Teams, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then ACs, no NFRs) with the inferred team assignments flagged for human verification. HLR-4's documentation requirement is met by the docs-authoring epic E002 per Rule 11.\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b26291dbe6906fec","agent_id":"a0166fef3b1463a0f","session_id":"2f248c86-604e-49da-86f8-c3023caf7896","uuid":"42a3b0d2-8bc4-4993-966e-ae8e2cb332c4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:50:59.044Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4f949d850caafbd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
